veloper-guy/buildkit-machine/tags,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/git/blobs{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/git/tags{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/git/refs{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/git/trees{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/statuses/{sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/languages,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/stargazers,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/contributors,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/subscribers,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/subscription,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/commits{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/git/commits{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/comments{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/issues/comments{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/contents/{+path},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/compare/{base}...{head},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/merges,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/{archive_format}{/ref},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/downloads,https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/issues{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/pulls{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/milestones{/number},"https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/notifications{?since,all,participating}",https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/labels{/name},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/releases{/id},https://api.github.com/repos/developer-guy/buildkit-machine/deployments,2022-01-08T18:44:26Z,2024-01-03T15:38:32Z,2025-12-05T02:42:29Z,git://github.com/developer-guy/buildkit-machine.git,git@github.com:developer-guy/buildkit-machine.git,https://github.com/developer-guy/buildkit-machine.git,https://github.com/developer-guy/buildkit-machine,https://batuhan-apaydin-11378.medium.com/buildkit-machine-a-brand-new-project-to-enable-building-pushing-container-images-without-requiring-f8a899fd0cd0,1437,56,56,Go,True,True,True,True,False,False,2,,False,False,3,"{'key': 'apache-2.0', 'name': 'Apache License 2.0', 'spdx_id': 'Apache-2.0', 'url': 'https://api.github.com/licenses/apache-2.0', 'node_id': 'MDc6TGljZW5zZTI='}",True,False,False,True,all,"['buildkit', 'buildkitd', 'containerd', 'lima', 'limactl', 'limavm', 'macos', 'moby', 'qemu']",public,2,3,56,master,"{'admin': False, 'maintain': False, 'push': False, 'triage': False, 'pull': True}",1.0,"# buildkit-machine

buildkit-machine allows you to make buildkitd daemon accessible in your macOS environment. To do so, it uses [lima](https://github.com/lima-vm/lima), which is a Linux subsystem for macOS, under the hood. lima spins up a VM that runs buildkitd daemon in a rootless way which means that sock file of the buildkitd daemon is now be able to accessible from `/run/user/<USERID>/buildkit/buildkitd`.

## Overview

![gif](./.res/anim.gif)

## Architecture

![svg](./.res/graphviz.svg)

## Installation

```shell
$ go install github.com/developer-guy/buildkit-machine@latest
```

## Usage

> Please ensure you've installed limactl because buildkit-machine will use limactl executable under the hood.

To make it accessible Buildkitd Daemon over socket:

```shell
$ buildkit-machine start buildkitd --unix $(pwd)/buildkitd.sock
```

To make it accessible Buildkitd Daemon over TCP connection:

```shell
$ buildkit-machine start builtkitd --tcp 9999
```

Once you make buildkitd accessible to your host, you can be able to use client tooling such as `buildctl` to start building and pushing container images. There is an on-going issue in [Docker Buildx](https://github.com/docker/buildx/issues/23) side to let Buildx to connect remote Buildkit daemon. Once it is ready, we can use buildx too.
