ps://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/tags,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/git/blobs{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/git/tags{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/git/refs{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/git/trees{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/statuses/{sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/languages,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/stargazers,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/contributors,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/subscribers,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/subscription,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/commits{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/git/commits{/sha},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/comments{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/issues/comments{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/contents/{+path},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/compare/{base}...{head},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/merges,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/{archive_format}{/ref},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/downloads,https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/issues{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/pulls{/number},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/milestones{/number},"https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/notifications{?since,all,participating}",https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/labels{/name},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/releases{/id},https://api.github.com/repos/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub/deployments,2025-06-13T21:49:14Z,2025-06-17T00:18:59Z,2025-06-16T17:57:03Z,git://github.com/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub.git,git@github.com:Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub.git,https://github.com/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub.git,https://github.com/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub,,33899,1,1,Jupyter Notebook,True,True,True,True,False,False,0,,False,False,0,,True,False,False,True,all,"['bcrp', 'opendata', 'peru']",public,0,0,1,main,"{'admin': False, 'maintain': False, 'push': False, 'triage': False, 'pull': True}",1.0,"# BCRP Series Downloader

Download and consolidate time series from the [Banco Central de Reserva del Perú (BCRP)](https://estadisticas.bcrp.gob.pe/estadisticas/series/ayuda/api) API. This tool scrapes metadata, downloads 16k+ series in async batches, and stores them as Parquet files for fast analytics.

---

## 🚀 Quick Start

1. **Install dependencies**

Clone the repository:
   ```sh
   git clone https://github.com/Tooruogata/bcrp-data-hub.git
   cd bcrp-data-hub
   ```

Set up the docker image:
   ```sh
   docker build -t bcrp-data-hub:latest -f .devcontainer/Dockerfile .
   docker run -dit --name bcrp-data-hub -v ""$repopath:/workspace"" -w /workspace bcrp-data-hub:latest
   ```

2. **Run script**

   ```python
   control_panel()  # Create control CSV from metadata

   await run_batch(
       df_control=df_control,
       formato=""json"",
       inicio=""2000-1"",
       fin=""2025-12"",
       idioma=""esp"",
       output_dir=""../data/bronze/"",
       batch_size=100
   )

   duckdb.sql(""""""
       COPY (
           SELECT * FROM read_parquet('../data/bronze/*.parquet')
       ) TO '../data/silver/series_all.parquet' (FORMAT PARQUET);
   """""")
   ```

---

## 📁 Structure

```text
project/
├── data/
│   ├── bronze/         # Raw per-series files (Parquet)
│   ├── silver/         # Consolidated Parquet dataset
│   └── metadata/       # Control panel CSV
├── pull_data.ipynb     # Notebook to pull and download
└── README.md
```

---

## 🧰 Features

* ✅ Scrapes official BCRP metadata
* ⚡ Async download of 16k+ series
* 📁 Saves individual files to `bronze/`
* 🧹 Merges all into `silver/series_all.parquet`
* ⏱️ \~5 min for 16k series, \~50s to consolidate

---

## 🔍 Query Example

```python
import duckdb

df = duckdb.sql(""SELECT * FROM read_parquet('../data/silver/series_all.parquet')"").df()
```
